              Pipeline job

   It is a job used to provide an enhanced way to model and visualize CI/CD workflow for a software delivery project.
   It is created by writting a bunch of instructions in a file called Jenkinsfile which can be checked into an SCM repository

   we have 2 rypes
      A declarative pipeline
      A Scripted pipeline

   Jenkins plugins are "java archives" with a .hpi/jpi extensions


  The different  stages in a Jenkins file
    1- Jenkins file have an agent: it specifies where the pipeline job will run e.g linux machine, windows machine (normally jenkins runs as a cluster with a 
                                   controller and slaves)
    2- stages : these show the acrual work of the CI/CD of the pipeline
    3- stage  : it is one of the stage
    4- steps  : each pipeline stage include steps
    5- Post build: used to send an email notification

     The Jenkins documentation gives samples of Jenkinsfile

     1- Jenkins controller: this is the machine where Jenkins is installed and centrally stores all the configurations, plugins. It loads the plugins, and renders 
                             a jenkins user interface. It makes sure that jobs can be deployed to the agent.  
     2- Agent : It is the machine that connects to the controler and performs various operations as directed by a jenkins controller
     3- Node: It allocates an executor to run a jenkins job
     4- Executor

